>>
>> mu'o mi'e la selpa'i
>
> I think it's a marked difference no matter how you think of lo and 
> da--{lo} definitely allows for referents to be in the universe of discourse 
> and not selected, whereas {da} does not. That is, {PA lo broda} takes 
> exactly PA things from {lo broda}, which might be quite small compared to 
> the whole UD worth of brodas. {PA broda} takes exactly PA things from the 
> entire UD worth of brodas. This is already far too technical for the 
> beginners list though.
>

Xorlophiles, please move to a separate thread. 


> mi'e la latro'a mu'o
